# generated EPUB editions + math spikes — build outputs, never source
*.epub

# Logs
*.log

# Item-collection files for temporary testing.  (These were one fused line,
# `*.tsv*.epub.sha256` — a pattern matching nothing — which is why both kinds
# kept surfacing as untracked.)
*.tsv
*.epub.sha256

# Corpus fingerprint for the viewer article-cache bust — build output, a hash of
# data/derived/articles (which is itself untracked).  A committed copy could not be
# verified from the repo and would go stale against the local corpus; deploy.sh
# regenerates it immediately before upload.
tools/viewer/build-stamp.js

# EPUBCheck, the TEI Consortium-independent validator we gate the books on.
# 32 MB of third-party jar — installed, not committed.  `tools/check_epub.sh`
# IS committed, knows this path, and prints the download URL when the jar is
# absent: the pair is what makes the tool findable from a fresh clone, which a
# jar sitting in a session scratchpad was not.
tools/epubcheck/

# The built books, their published checksums, and the build logs.  `*.epub`
# already ignored the files; this ignores the DIRECTORY, which is the thing
# deploy.sh now mkdir -p's.  ~800 MB of dead July probe builds used to sit
# loose in the repo root beside them; the two books we ship are all that is left.
epub/
